35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission trial worked, but the joint clinic failed because neither department held the budget.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The booking system only records named slots. Unfixed work disappears from reports.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The joint clinic closed because neither side carried the rota. The data agreements take fourteen months.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Nine nursing posts are unfilled. Agency cover is eating the pay bill. Midwifery has slack.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,The development allocation is down a quarter. Off-site contacts draw no tariff from the fund.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the joint clinic failure is a warning. We cannot rely on shared rotas.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, if it is not in the booking system, it does not exist for us.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Servas, if off-site work earns nothing, we are subsidizing it with on-site revenue.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, the booking system is rigid. But the midwifery slack is a real opportunity.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, the slack is useful, but the budget is shrinking. We must be precise.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,The readmission data proves home visits work. But the joint clinic shows shared governance fails.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The parking fills before eleven. The shuttle misses most villages. On-site is the only viable option.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The data agreements are a bottleneck. Any program relying on outside surgeries is doomed.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,The therapy staff are leaving. But midwifery has room. We should use that slack.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,The tariffs confirm on-site is the only way to earn back the cost. Off-site is a loss.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,We need a program that is self-contained and on-site to avoid the joint clinic trap.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,It must fit into the existing booking slots. No new infrastructure that seizes up.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,It must not rely on outside data agreements. It must be internally managed.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,It must use the midwifery slack. We cannot add to the nursing burden.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,It must be on-site to generate tariff revenue. The budget cannot support off-site losses.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
